WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.429
The lowest common multiple is the smallest
positive number

2
00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:06.842
that appears in both numbers' times
tables.

3
00:00:07.535 --> 00:00:09.768
We call it the L C M.

4
00:00:10.298 --> 00:00:12.345
Let's find it for four and six.

5
00:00:13.003 --> 00:00:16.883
Multiples of four are four, eight, twelve,
sixteen, and

6
00:00:16.893 --> 00:00:21.363
so on. Multiples of six are six, twelve,
eighteen, and

7
00:00:21.373 --> 00:00:26.149
so on. Twelve is the first positive number
in both lists.

8
00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:31.223
So twelve is the lowest common multiple of
four and six.

9
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.439
That helps us add one quarter and one
sixth.

10
00:00:34.771 --> 00:00:36.528
We need equal-sized parts.

11
00:00:36.884 --> 00:00:40.810
Twelve is a useful common denominator
because both four

12
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.717
and six divide into twelve.

13
00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.863
Multiply both numbers in one quarter by
three.

14
00:00:46.126 --> 00:00:48.324
One quarter equals three twelfths.

15
00:00:48.704 --> 00:00:51.608
Multiplying the numerator and denominator
by the same

16
00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:55.290
number keeps the fraction's value
unchanged.

17
00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.119
For one sixth, multiply the numerator and
denominator

18
00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:02.497
by two. One sixth equals two twelfths.

19
00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:05.899
These fractions now use the same-sized
parts.

20
00:01:06.278 --> 00:01:08.511
Add three twelfths and two twelfths.

21
00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:10.496
That makes five twelfths.

22
00:01:10.852 --> 00:01:12.505
Keep the denominator twelve.

23
00:01:12.675 --> 00:01:15.245
The answer is already in simplest form.

24
00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:19.109
Remember: find the shared multiples,
choose the smallest

25
00:01:19.119 --> 00:01:22.106
positive one, rename, then calculate.

26
00:01:22.311 --> 00:01:25.308
Any common denominator can work, but the
lowest common

27
00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.481
multiple usually keeps the numbers
smaller.

